<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>TURKU, Finland 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the world ice hockey championships on Tuesday:</p>
<p>Pool B</p>
<p>Sweden 4 Norway 1 (0-1 2-0 2-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Sweden - Marcus Ragnarsson (25:38), Per Eklund (31:48), Michael</p>
<p>Nylander (40:17), Mattias Ohlund (45:41)</p>
<p>Norway - Matts Trygg (14:32)</p>
<p>Penalties:</p>
<p>Sweden 16 minutes, Norway 8</p>
<p>Attendance: 3,882</p>
<p>Group A (in Helsinki):</p>
<p>Germany 0 Finland 6 (0-2 0-2 0-2)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Finland - Saku Koivu (01:10), Mika Stromberg (19:34, 37:50), Marko Jantunen (23:04), Janne Ojanen (46:11), Olli Jokinen (47:59).</p>
<p>Penalties: Germany 12 minutes, Finland 8 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 13,243</p>
